            <ArticleTitle>Opioid hyperexcitability: the application of alternate opioid therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>353-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three cases are reported where patients experienced severe central nervous system adverse effects on high-dose hydromorphone. These effects were rapidly alleviated following a change in therapy to morphine at 20-25% of the usually accepted potency equivalent dose. We recommend caution in using equivalent dose tables when changing opioid therapy in patients receiving high-dose opioid treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
